Just tell them that the first one to solve the riddle gets their paper published.

01:07:43.539 --> 01:07:46.659
Yeah, then you might have not, then you might have too much blood.

01:07:47.139 --> 01:07:47.779
That's true.

01:07:48.099 --> 01:07:48.579
All right.

01:07:49.139 --> 01:07:50.899
Does anyone take it?

01:07:53.299 --> 01:07:55.779
I'm not actually evil, so I'm going to start with ink.

01:07:57.299 --> 01:07:59.699
I ask around for right.

01:07:59.779 --> 01:08:02.500
So, you know, everybody starting pulls out pouches of ink, right?

01:08:02.659 --> 01:08:10.019
Because, of course, like, you know, if you're a scholar, you, you know, there's you pick when you which one.

01:08:10.659 --> 01:08:10.979
Yeah.

01:08:11.539 --> 01:08:15.779
So I'll take whatever looks freshest.

01:08:16.099 --> 01:08:16.500
All right.

01:08:16.659 --> 01:08:29.460
So you pour it in, and then you hear the grinding of stone as the statue slides forwards on its dais to reveal a long set of stairs leading down an unlit passage.

01:08:29.779 --> 01:08:30.420
Ooh, this is cool.

01:08:30.659 --> 01:08:32.739
So, how long has the statue been here?

01:08:34.340 --> 01:08:37.300
Well, you really are going to make me look this up.

01:08:37.619 --> 01:08:39.380
No, I'm just like a long time, right?

01:08:39.699 --> 01:08:40.260
Yes.

01:08:40.899 --> 01:08:43.139
And nobody over all that time has put ink in the ink.

01:08:43.219 --> 01:08:44.019
Well, I'm just saying.

01:08:44.099 --> 01:08:45.219
It's a little on the notes.

01:08:45.939 --> 01:08:48.260
I mean, maybe they haven't done it with intent.

01:08:48.579 --> 01:08:48.819
Okay.

01:08:49.939 --> 01:08:50.500
I'm just saying.

01:08:53.380 --> 01:08:56.579
The minute you say that, they all kind of look at you in horror.

01:08:57.219 --> 01:08:59.300
Like, why would we deface the thing?

01:08:59.619 --> 01:09:00.019
Yes, yes.

01:09:00.099 --> 01:09:00.739
You know, there's like this.

01:09:01.219 --> 01:09:03.300
Wasn't it like there's something else hidden in a statue earlier?

01:09:03.460 --> 01:09:07.059
I mean, like, we put stuff in statues, like, you know, little things all the time, right?

01:09:07.219 --> 01:09:08.340
I mean, like, oh, go ahead.

01:09:08.819 --> 01:09:09.539
Okay, I'm not going to.

01:09:10.019 --> 01:09:12.420
Yeah, he's, you know, they're all kind of like looking at you.

01:09:12.500 --> 01:09:15.139
Like, this would be, you know, Olwando's like, no, apparently nobody had that.

01:09:15.300 --> 01:09:15.859
All right, all right.

01:09:15.939 --> 01:09:16.099
All right.

01:09:16.340 --> 01:09:17.139
Let's keep going.

01:09:17.460 --> 01:09:17.779
All right.

01:09:18.099 --> 01:09:20.659
But, but, you know, good plot hole, good plot hole discovery.

01:09:20.899 --> 01:09:21.460
All right.

01:09:21.779 --> 01:09:21.939
Okay.

01:09:22.019 --> 01:09:23.859
So there's a bunch of stairs going down.

01:09:27.859 --> 01:09:30.899
How many years did he live?

01:09:31.059 --> 01:09:32.500
It says we should go down that many steps.

01:09:32.899 --> 01:09:33.380
Everybody died.

01:09:33.460 --> 01:09:34.019
TPK.

01:09:34.739 --> 01:09:36.179
Apparently, thank you.

01:09:36.340 --> 01:09:40.420
My wife got me some food, which is good because I was getting really hungry.

01:09:41.139 --> 01:09:45.219
So it turns out nobody actually knows when he died, how old he was when he died.

01:09:48.819 --> 01:09:48.979
Okay.

01:09:49.859 --> 01:09:50.100
Pause.

01:09:50.180 --> 01:09:50.420
Pause.

01:09:50.500 --> 01:09:50.899
Pause.

01:09:51.060 --> 01:09:51.220
Yeah.

01:09:51.380 --> 01:09:53.779
Because that's not considered important information.

01:09:54.100 --> 01:10:01.140
But fortunately, there is a copy of his biography.

01:10:03.619 --> 01:10:05.460
It's not listed on his statue?

01:10:05.699 --> 01:10:09.939
I mean, that's a pretty deficient plaque.

01:10:10.260 --> 01:10:12.579
Yeah, well, you know, it's one of those things.

01:10:14.340 --> 01:10:17.699
So one of you can head over.

01:10:17.859 --> 01:10:26.579
You can all rush over to the House of Momentous Deeds where the volume Olwando of the Wonders has the answer, or you can start going down the stairs and take your luck.

01:10:27.300 --> 01:10:28.739
I mean, I kind of eyeball it.

01:10:29.539 --> 01:10:32.020
Is it a very long staircase?

01:10:32.180 --> 01:10:34.260
Or, I mean, does it just go down a couple of steps?

01:10:34.579 --> 01:10:39.140
I'm afraid if we go one step too far, like, you know, I don't know, like, statues come alive and shit, right?

01:10:40.100 --> 01:10:43.140
Yeah, it'll kill us with a quill.

01:10:43.460 --> 01:10:43.779
Yeah.

01:10:44.739 --> 01:10:54.100
Well, you know, let's go ahead and at this point in time, you've managed to acquire quite a retinue of people, right?

01:10:54.579 --> 01:10:57.220
Scribbling notes, everybody, you know, discussing.

01:10:58.020 --> 01:11:01.220
You're apparently getting the impression that this will be studied for years.

01:11:01.539 --> 01:11:05.460
The part where Thorin solved the puzzle is what's causing everybody to be excited.

01:11:07.060 --> 01:11:12.899
I make a little speech explaining so that at least some of it is likely to be written down correctly.

01:11:13.220 --> 01:11:13.539
Okay.

01:11:16.390 --> 01:11:16.870
All right.

01:11:17.750 --> 01:11:18.710
You find the book.

01:11:19.030 --> 01:11:19.670
All right.

01:11:23.190 --> 01:11:31.030
The other option is to go to the, and of course, as you're going there, one of the, once somebody says, oh, wait, I have a better solution.

01:11:31.670 --> 01:11:35.190
We could go to the grove where every keeper of tomes is buried.

01:11:37.750 --> 01:11:39.190
Are we going to dig him up and ask him?

01:11:39.430 --> 01:11:40.070
No, no, no.

01:11:42.230 --> 01:11:44.310
How old he lived is written down there.

01:11:44.790 --> 01:11:45.190
Okay, yeah.

01:11:45.510 --> 01:11:46.470
That's a better idea.

01:11:46.790 --> 01:11:47.190
All right.

01:11:47.350 --> 01:11:47.670
Okay.

01:11:47.990 --> 01:11:54.230
So off you head to the grove and there you find his body and discover that he died at the age of 97.

01:11:55.190 --> 01:11:55.590
All right.

01:11:55.830 --> 01:11:57.510
So 97 steps down the stairs.

01:11:57.670 --> 01:11:57.990
Okay.

01:11:59.910 --> 01:12:00.470
All right.

01:12:04.800 --> 01:12:08.400
Do we know the original prophecy?

01:12:14.250 --> 01:12:17.289
I'm just saying before we walk down 97 and then say, what's the prophecy?

01:12:17.370 --> 01:12:18.810
And they have to walk 97 back up.

01:12:18.890 --> 01:12:21.130
I'm just saying that's a lot of stairs to walk.

01:12:21.450 --> 01:12:25.130
Well, so the good news is that every scholar in Candlekeep knows this one by heart.

01:12:25.289 --> 01:12:29.370
And since you've managed to make so many friends, they'll let us know.

01:12:29.690 --> 01:12:30.570
They'll let you know.

01:12:30.810 --> 01:12:40.170
It also happens to be in yeah, so this is one of those things where you're able to pull it off.

01:12:40.250 --> 01:12:46.170
And thanks to all of your great work at helping people and generally being supportive, you have it.

01:12:46.410 --> 01:12:46.730
Okay.

01:12:47.050 --> 01:12:53.930
So from knowledge of what scholars want, I make sure that everyone knows who lent me the ink.

01:12:54.490 --> 01:12:54.890
All right.

01:13:00.900 --> 01:13:04.180
He makes sure that everybody knows the correct spelling of his name.

01:13:04.500 --> 01:13:04.740
Yeah.

01:13:06.260 --> 01:13:08.580
He wants to get credit and citations.

01:13:11.700 --> 01:13:12.100
All right.

01:13:16.529 --> 01:13:16.689
Okay.

01:13:17.090 --> 01:13:21.170
So where do you want to stand when you read the citation when you read the prophecy?

01:13:24.060 --> 01:13:24.380
Oh.

01:13:25.100 --> 01:13:26.779
97 steps down.

01:13:31.970 --> 01:13:32.449
Let's see.

01:13:32.609 --> 01:13:34.770
Tread as many steps as he lived in years.

01:13:34.930 --> 01:13:38.050
Utter the original prophecy to unseen ears.

01:13:40.529 --> 01:13:42.130
Unseen ears.

01:13:48.220 --> 01:13:50.539
It could mean nothing in particular.

01:13:50.859 --> 01:13:56.699
I mean, do we see anything of note or just standstairs?

01:13:56.940 --> 01:13:57.100
Yeah.

01:13:58.699 --> 01:14:05.100
Well, let's go 97 steps down and read the prophecy.

01:14:05.659 --> 01:14:07.659
Oh, do we have the dust?

01:14:07.819 --> 01:14:08.539
We need dust.

01:14:08.779 --> 01:14:10.300
Dust of Mechanus.

01:14:10.539 --> 01:14:11.420
Mechanis.

01:14:12.380 --> 01:14:12.699
Oh.

01:14:17.890 --> 01:14:22.210
Oh, yeah, that's one of those where I probably got the J and the K, the C.

01:14:24.130 --> 01:14:24.369
Yeah.

01:14:24.930 --> 01:14:25.650
Mechanis.

01:14:28.320 --> 01:14:35.840
You know, it says those well-versed in Candlekeep's lore may fearlessly pass the obsidian door.

01:14:37.440 --> 01:14:40.640
Should we don't actually know it that well?

01:14:41.200 --> 01:14:42.880
Who knows it best?

01:14:43.200 --> 01:14:46.800
We have an entire entourage of scholars living in Candlekeep.

01:14:47.039 --> 01:14:48.640
Won't they all be experts?

01:14:49.520 --> 01:14:51.680
Not all of them are experts on the.

01:14:52.320 --> 01:14:55.920
I'm sure there's some who know it better than others.

01:14:56.240 --> 01:14:58.480
Like there must be a specialty in local history.

01:14:58.800 --> 01:15:01.360
I mean, you could ask and see who volunteers.

01:15:01.680 --> 01:15:02.160
Well, yeah, yeah.

01:15:02.400 --> 01:15:03.200
I'm asking.

01:15:04.720 --> 01:15:09.039
Who are the experts on the Candlekeep itself?

01:15:09.840 --> 01:15:10.160
Okay.

01:15:10.880 --> 01:15:15.840
I'm just imagining everybody raising their hand and screaming their qualifications.

01:15:17.760 --> 01:15:18.320
All right.

01:15:18.960 --> 01:15:19.920
To make this modest.

01:15:20.800 --> 01:15:23.120
A lot of these would have scorn for local history.

01:15:23.760 --> 01:15:25.280
It's not their specialty.

01:15:25.920 --> 01:15:26.880
Actually, that's a good point.

01:15:27.200 --> 01:15:28.320
That seems like something that...

01:15:28.560 --> 01:15:32.079
Okay, so I think it would be more amusing if you have the.

01:15:33.120 --> 01:15:34.800
So you know a guy.

01:15:35.440 --> 01:15:35.920
Ah.

01:15:37.120 --> 01:15:37.920
You know a guy.

01:15:38.320 --> 01:15:42.640
We've definitely talked to a lot of people while we've been here, so we've probably picked up on those who know the key.

01:15:43.200 --> 01:15:48.560
So you do manage to acquire one of the scholars who happens to be familiar with the area.

01:15:48.880 --> 01:16:02.800
So he's very excited about the opportunity to come with you and ask whether he can just take a moment to go get some few things and knobs and nabs.

01:16:03.680 --> 01:16:06.000
Yeah, does he have the dust of Mechanus?

01:16:06.640 --> 01:16:08.640
No, unfortunately, the dust of Mechanus.

01:16:09.120 --> 01:16:11.520
Mechanist is a particular plane, so.

01:16:14.000 --> 01:16:16.960
Oh, we might be in trouble if we can't get some.

01:16:21.120 --> 01:16:26.079
And unless it's just some sort of dry lubricant, it kind of implies that it is.

01:16:26.560 --> 01:16:29.360
It says to sprinkle it on dormant gears.

01:16:32.320 --> 01:16:32.640
So.

01:16:38.270 --> 01:16:41.470
Is the dust of Mechanist Coke?

01:16:42.510 --> 01:16:42.830
No.

01:16:44.350 --> 01:16:46.270
That would be an expensive lubricant.

01:16:46.510 --> 01:16:47.550
I'm just saying.

01:16:51.230 --> 01:16:52.990
So who goes?

01:16:58.910 --> 01:17:12.190
So he goes, well, Mechanus happens to be a plane is one of the planes of one of the planes in the cosmic wheel.

01:17:13.710 --> 01:17:21.630
And the dust of Mechanus could be anything.

01:17:21.790 --> 01:17:24.670
It could be dust from that plane.

01:17:24.830 --> 01:17:28.430
It could be dust from, it could be, you know, killing one of those creatures.

01:17:28.590 --> 01:17:33.710
Whenever they die, they turn into dust because they're not from this, they're not from the prime material plane.

01:17:35.310 --> 01:17:36.270
Have we killed one of those?

01:17:36.350 --> 01:17:37.470
Can we get one of those?

01:17:42.400 --> 01:17:42.720
Let's see.

01:17:42.880 --> 01:17:46.079
Can we ask Glabbagool if he has any squirreled away somewhere?

01:17:47.760 --> 01:17:50.000
Glabbagool says, no, I do not.

01:17:53.520 --> 01:17:57.360
I ask whether it's any relation to the dust of Suleiman.

01:17:58.239 --> 01:17:59.119
No, no, it's not.

01:17:59.199 --> 01:17:59.520
Hold on.

01:18:00.079 --> 01:18:02.319
But they do point out that I just need to check something.

01:18:02.480 --> 01:18:03.680
Give me one second.

01:18:15.789 --> 01:18:21.150
I mean, the description really makes it sound like it's a form of preventative maintenance for these gears.

01:18:21.470 --> 01:18:26.350
Yes, so that's another option.

01:18:26.430 --> 01:18:28.989
You can try to see if you actually do need it.

01:18:30.590 --> 01:18:34.510
I mean, can someone plane shift us and we just go kill some stuff and come back?

01:18:34.829 --> 01:18:38.270
Well, I mean, it turns out, so the house of, it turns out there is a house of Mechanus.

01:18:38.350 --> 01:18:44.110
It's a large rectangular with a blue straight loof, a roof, and a pended clock tower.

01:18:44.350 --> 01:18:47.150
It sits between the immortal chambers and Founders' Court.

01:18:47.310 --> 01:18:51.150
It is a library dedicated to construction, engineering, and technology.

01:18:53.239 --> 01:19:00.439
Apparently, there are 13 modrons that are currently working there under the direction of Spanner, the librarian.

01:19:01.399 --> 01:19:02.520
Sorry, 13 whats?

01:19:02.840 --> 01:19:03.560
Modrons.

01:19:03.640 --> 01:19:05.319
Those are creatures from that plane.

01:19:05.640 --> 01:19:08.920
Oh, so I don't want to kill any of them if they're just librarians.

01:19:09.000 --> 01:19:09.399
I don't kill them.

01:19:10.119 --> 01:19:10.680
Why do we have to kill them?

01:19:11.079 --> 01:19:11.800
Do they like sneeze?

01:19:11.880 --> 01:19:13.399
Does it like sneeze dust or something?

01:19:13.560 --> 01:19:14.359
I mean, like, you know.

01:19:15.079 --> 01:19:19.720
I think we can just ask them for their advice or, you know, if they've got a bag of dust that we can borrow.

01:19:20.039 --> 01:19:20.680
All right.

01:19:22.199 --> 01:19:23.640
Yes, they do not need to kill them.

01:19:23.880 --> 01:19:25.880
That is one of many solutions to the problem.

01:19:26.359 --> 01:19:27.640
Presumably, they're academics.

01:19:28.119 --> 01:19:29.640
I mean, we don't kill librarians.

01:19:29.960 --> 01:19:30.199
No.

01:19:30.520 --> 01:19:31.640
They're our friends.

01:19:32.520 --> 01:19:34.359
Haven't we killed a librarian before?

01:19:34.680 --> 01:19:36.279
But they attacked us first.

01:19:36.920 --> 01:19:38.680
I'm sure it was justified.

01:19:40.840 --> 01:19:50.279
Baz remembers that in the book that Milo wrote, they actually had the, what was it, the gift from the librarian letter or something?

01:19:50.600 --> 01:19:52.359
Yeah, yes, yes.

01:19:57.640 --> 01:20:00.199
He muses that something like that would be useful now.

01:20:00.760 --> 01:20:01.239
Yes.

01:20:02.840 --> 01:20:03.159
Okay.

01:20:07.989 --> 01:20:08.630
All right.

01:20:09.909 --> 01:20:10.229
Okay.

01:20:10.789 --> 01:20:16.310
So you arrive at the at his at their, where they're located.

01:20:16.630 --> 01:20:22.229
And modrons, let me just make sure if I don't accidentally tell you the wrong description.

01:20:22.550 --> 01:20:26.630
Let me just show there should be a way for me to do this.

01:20:31.140 --> 01:20:35.539
If I spell it correctly, no, of course I didn't, because that would have been too easy.

01:20:37.779 --> 01:20:38.659
Modron.

01:20:40.260 --> 01:20:42.420
Ah, I did spell it correctly.

01:20:43.380 --> 01:20:45.300
Ah, why did that change?

01:20:47.460 --> 01:20:51.940
Anyway, a modron, so it's like a box with two hands and little eyes.

01:20:55.670 --> 01:20:56.149
Sounds cute.

01:20:56.310 --> 01:20:57.270
Is it cute?

01:20:58.229 --> 01:20:58.869
Sounds like a little roll.

01:20:59.189 --> 01:20:59.829
Bemo?

01:21:01.109 --> 01:21:01.350
Let's see.

01:21:01.829 --> 01:21:03.029
Do you know who Bemo is?

01:21:03.590 --> 01:21:03.909
No.

01:21:04.470 --> 01:21:05.270
Who is he?

01:21:05.590 --> 01:21:07.750
From, oh God, it's from a cartoon.

01:21:08.069 --> 01:21:08.310
Oh.

01:21:11.119 --> 01:21:11.680
All right.

01:21:11.920 --> 01:21:13.039
From Adventure Time.

01:21:13.359 --> 01:21:14.319
Adventure Time, man.

01:21:18.630 --> 01:21:20.389
No, I do not want this.

01:21:21.029 --> 01:21:21.909
No, go away.

01:21:22.069 --> 01:21:22.309
Stop.

01:21:22.470 --> 01:21:22.710
Stop.

01:21:22.869 --> 01:21:23.189
Stop.

01:21:23.510 --> 01:21:25.029
I'm pretty sure they're like Bemo.

01:21:25.590 --> 01:21:27.670
Here, I'll put that in the Discord, too.

01:21:27.909 --> 01:21:29.670
All I'm doing is sending images your way.

01:21:29.829 --> 01:21:30.229
There we go.

01:21:30.389 --> 01:21:31.269
That's Bemo.

01:21:32.229 --> 01:21:32.869
All right.

01:21:33.510 --> 01:21:33.750
Okay.

01:21:33.909 --> 01:21:41.909
So if you want to know what they are, I just put a link in the Zoom chat which points to them.

01:21:42.550 --> 01:21:44.869
Oh, which one?

01:21:45.029 --> 01:21:47.510
And then the role chat 20 chat.

01:21:47.829 --> 01:21:48.229
Oh, wow.

01:21:49.429 --> 01:21:50.470
That's pretty much Bemo.

01:21:50.630 --> 01:21:51.829
They look hilarious.

01:21:52.149 --> 01:21:52.309
Yeah.

01:21:53.269 --> 01:21:55.510
Not as cute as I was hoping, but okay.

01:21:56.470 --> 01:21:57.029
I don't know.

01:21:57.109 --> 01:21:59.429
I like the one that looks like two stack boxes.

01:22:01.269 --> 01:22:02.869
Got a creepy face.

01:22:04.389 --> 01:22:04.710
Yeah.

01:22:08.360 --> 01:22:09.000
All right.

01:22:10.279 --> 01:22:12.279
So, yes.

01:22:12.440 --> 01:22:14.840
So it's kind of like a box with hands.

01:22:17.079 --> 01:22:17.720
They are.

01:22:18.840 --> 01:22:23.560
So Spanner is sitting there looking at you.

01:22:24.440 --> 01:22:27.480
The thing about Mechanis is that it's all very mechanical.

01:22:27.560 --> 01:22:30.760
So everybody's moving in tight circles.

01:22:31.640 --> 01:22:33.319
Everything is carefully organized.

01:22:33.480 --> 01:22:37.610
It's sort of like an OCD person's wet dream.

01:22:40.490 --> 01:22:43.289
The GNOME looks at you and asks you, what are you looking for?

01:22:43.450 --> 01:22:45.289
What is it that you're hoping to get?

01:22:46.890 --> 01:22:53.690
Well, we believe we have a situation where we need to lubricate some machinery.

01:22:54.010 --> 01:23:03.289
And the suggested lubricant was dust of Mechanus, and we thought you might have a line on some.

01:23:04.810 --> 01:23:16.490
Well, he pauses and says, well, it is a well-known fact that the dust from the plane of Mechanis is, in fact, the most perfect of all lubricants.

01:23:20.439 --> 01:23:24.039
Well, how may we obtain some?

01:23:26.679 --> 01:23:28.599
We appreciate its positive qualities.

01:23:28.920 --> 01:23:30.759
He goes, that's an excellent question.

01:23:31.079 --> 01:23:37.159
So there are two known ways to secure such a thing.

01:23:38.119 --> 01:23:39.399
One of them asking politely.

01:23:41.619 --> 01:23:43.699
There's a stunned moment of silence.

01:23:44.020 --> 01:23:46.020
It's not polite when you interrupt.

01:23:46.340 --> 01:23:47.220
Oh, I'm sorry.

01:23:48.100 --> 01:23:48.900
Please continue.

01:23:49.380 --> 01:23:50.180
I apologize.

01:23:50.659 --> 01:23:57.140
I mean, sorry, you've come to his place of work, and you're not going to give him an opportunity to meander for at least 10 minutes.

01:23:57.860 --> 01:24:08.500
Well, I actually don't know how urgent it is, but there might be a villain prepared to do villainous things if we're not in a hurry.

01:24:08.820 --> 01:24:09.060
All right.

01:24:09.220 --> 01:24:09.699
So, roll your.

01:24:10.100 --> 01:24:10.180
Okay.

01:24:10.260 --> 01:24:14.659
So, there's he basically boils down to one of two approaches.

01:24:15.300 --> 01:24:17.860
The first is you can.

01:24:19.220 --> 01:24:28.739
So, he goes, the only way to obtain dust from the plane of Mechanus would be to kill one of my modrons, which is absolutely unacceptable.

01:24:29.300 --> 01:24:37.300
A second attempt, a second approach, might be to use some special tools my modrons have, in fact, created.

01:24:39.940 --> 01:24:41.060
That sounds like a better option.

01:24:41.860 --> 01:24:42.500
Let's try it.

01:24:42.820 --> 01:24:48.340
Although, is it ever awkward that you're full of extremely valuable things?

01:24:49.539 --> 01:24:51.779
Up until today, it has never been an issue.

01:24:52.100 --> 01:24:52.659
Oh, okay.

01:24:53.140 --> 01:24:53.539
That's good.

01:24:54.260 --> 01:24:55.460
We won't make it an issue.

01:24:55.779 --> 01:24:56.500
Yes, he goes.

01:24:56.659 --> 01:25:00.020
Now, the problem is that these are very unique and special items.

01:25:00.659 --> 01:25:01.539
The tools?

01:25:01.860 --> 01:25:03.380
Yes, the tools.

01:25:04.340 --> 01:25:08.289
And so I will need something for collateral.

01:25:09.489 --> 01:25:11.170
We don't need to keep the tools.

01:25:11.329 --> 01:25:12.849
We just need the dust.

01:25:14.449 --> 01:25:17.409
He pauses and says, But what guarantee will I have that the tool?

01:25:17.889 --> 01:25:20.449
There's like this pause, sort of like, you know, he's very confused.

01:25:20.609 --> 01:25:25.089
Roll your persuasion because that was a very good idea.

01:25:27.409 --> 01:25:30.449
Joe, my persuasion is negative one, so you guys tell me what.

01:25:30.689 --> 01:25:31.250
Oh, well.

01:25:31.889 --> 01:25:33.809
I'll do my 14.

01:25:35.089 --> 01:25:35.489
All right.

01:25:35.809 --> 01:25:36.449
I'll do mine.

01:25:36.529 --> 01:25:37.409
What do we got here?

01:25:38.289 --> 01:25:39.729
I need to reload.

01:25:45.739 --> 01:25:53.819
He accepts the offer, but insists that Zalthir and Glabbagool have to.

01:25:54.299 --> 01:26:02.779
He wants to study Zalthir and Glabbagool's construction for its perfect symmetry, mechanical symmetry,

01:26:05.189 --> 01:26:11.269
and says that he's willing to give it as long as Zalthir and Glabbagool are willing to sit through a brief interview.

01:26:14.659 --> 01:26:15.299
We are.

01:26:15.779 --> 01:26:17.139
I consult with Glabbagool.

01:26:17.539 --> 01:26:27.539
We're game as long as you give us constructive feedback, such that we may better symbiotically serve our Zen cause.

01:26:30.579 --> 01:26:32.739
I'll always, always be selling.

01:26:34.419 --> 01:26:36.259
I'll keep that in mind.

01:26:37.539 --> 01:26:43.459
But they'll have to wait until after you go through this because the question and answer period will be quite complicated.

01:26:43.619 --> 01:26:55.299
But yes, he sort of turns around and speaks in this mechanistic language that you can't really possibly understand and can't even figure out how a GNOME is actually able to make those sounds.

01:26:55.619 --> 01:27:05.539
At which point in time, all the modrons sort of engage in sort of a hypothetical, you assume, are talking to each other as they kind of move their arms and bodies around in sort of a mechanized dance.

01:27:05.779 --> 01:27:08.579
It's all very, very, very creepy.

01:27:11.859 --> 01:27:20.419
With that piece of information, with that, you guys can head down the stairs to the, you can now head down the stairs.

01:27:20.659 --> 01:27:20.899
All right.

01:27:20.979 --> 01:27:21.779
So what step are you going to?

01:27:22.659 --> 01:27:24.579
Did we make the dust already?

01:27:24.899 --> 01:27:27.859
No, you have the tool, which is an alternative.

01:27:29.059 --> 01:27:31.779
So I feel like there's a trick question because it's like he's 97 years old.

01:27:31.939 --> 01:27:32.579
You're like, what, Stephen?

01:27:32.659 --> 01:27:33.299
We said 97.

01:27:33.459 --> 01:27:34.019
You keep asking us.

01:27:34.179 --> 01:27:35.699
Is there something else we should know?

01:27:37.299 --> 01:27:38.179
I'm the GM.

01:27:38.259 --> 01:27:42.419
That's my job to ask you where you were precisely standing before someone.

01:27:42.899 --> 01:27:44.019
I'm suspicious.

01:27:44.579 --> 01:27:48.659
I go down 97 steps and I keep my distance.

01:27:48.979 --> 01:27:49.379
All right.

01:27:50.979 --> 01:27:52.979
And I recite the prophecy.

01:27:53.299 --> 01:27:54.579
Oh, is it Zalthir?

01:27:56.639 --> 01:27:57.679
Are you standing next to him?

01:27:57.920 --> 01:27:59.199
Like, where are you standing relative to the staff?

01:27:59.359 --> 01:28:00.719
I'll be on 97.

01:28:01.359 --> 01:28:01.920
All right.

01:28:03.359 --> 01:28:04.159
Are they big steps?

01:28:04.399 --> 01:28:07.519
No, I mean, like, you can be a 96 or 95, but not a 97.

01:28:07.759 --> 01:28:08.960
I mean, two of you can be on it.

01:28:09.119 --> 01:28:12.319
Like, all four of you, if you squeeze in and like are nice and cuddly with each other.

01:28:12.559 --> 01:28:14.960
Yeah, I guess the question is above or below.

01:28:16.000 --> 01:28:17.439
I mean, I can also fly.

01:28:17.599 --> 01:28:19.519
Like, oh, hover.

01:28:19.679 --> 01:28:20.319
Very nice.

01:28:20.879 --> 01:28:21.920
You could hover, right?

01:28:23.119 --> 01:28:23.359
Right.

01:28:23.519 --> 01:28:24.799
And you have a potion of flying.

01:28:27.119 --> 01:28:29.279
Daz, what are you going to do?

01:28:30.960 --> 01:28:32.319
I mean, could I just.

01:28:32.719 --> 01:28:33.839
No, where are you going to sit?

01:28:33.920 --> 01:28:37.119
Are you going to stand on the stair or above, below?

01:28:38.319 --> 01:28:40.159
Where's my health right now?

01:28:40.479 --> 01:28:41.039
I'm good.

01:28:41.199 --> 01:28:42.559
I'm like, I can go anywhere.

01:28:42.960 --> 01:28:47.439
I'll having clear view and letting ranged weapons hit would be good.

01:28:47.599 --> 01:28:49.039
So I'll stay a little high.

01:28:50.159 --> 01:28:53.199
Seat 96, 95, 93, 92, 90.

01:28:54.239 --> 01:28:55.679
You're going to like stay low?

01:28:57.359 --> 01:28:58.559
I'm just asking, man.

01:28:59.119 --> 01:28:59.599
I don't know.

01:29:01.599 --> 01:29:08.399
While Mike is pondering, I think anytime you ask questions like this, it's followed by roll for initiative.

01:29:08.879 --> 01:29:12.319
Yeah, it's like it's going to be like, okay, your positions are locked in.

01:29:12.479 --> 01:29:13.359
Roll for initiative.

01:29:14.239 --> 01:29:15.759
It's hard to tell sometimes in the industry.

01:29:16.639 --> 01:29:19.279
I'll take up the rear in case somebody attacks us from behind.

01:29:20.319 --> 01:29:21.199
My stuff is pretty good.

01:29:21.519 --> 01:29:26.399
And if I'm at the top of the stairs, I'll be able to see with my ranged attacks.

01:29:27.119 --> 01:29:33.199
And I think if something's going to happen, I might as well be at the front because I can freaking tank it, but still.

01:29:33.679 --> 01:29:34.159
All right.

01:29:34.799 --> 01:29:37.199
Did we have a short rest in there somewhere?

01:29:38.159 --> 01:29:40.000
We have not, as far as I know.

01:29:40.319 --> 01:29:40.559
No.

01:29:41.920 --> 01:29:43.119
No short rest.

01:29:43.439 --> 01:29:43.839
Yes.

01:29:44.479 --> 01:29:48.559
So before we do this, can someone give me a quick heal?

01:29:49.199 --> 01:29:49.519
Sure.

01:29:49.759 --> 01:29:49.920
Yeah.

01:29:50.399 --> 01:29:52.000
How much could you use?

01:29:52.319 --> 01:29:53.839
I'm sure 27.

01:29:54.159 --> 01:29:55.199
Oh, yeah.

01:29:55.359 --> 01:29:57.279
Let me find a good one then.

01:30:03.350 --> 01:30:03.910
All right.

01:30:05.350 --> 01:30:05.910
24.

01:30:08.230 --> 01:30:09.110
I'm waiting for it.

01:30:09.270 --> 01:30:09.910
It's coming.

01:30:11.670 --> 01:30:12.070
All right.

01:30:12.390 --> 01:30:12.950
Actually, no.

01:30:13.190 --> 01:30:13.430
All right.

01:30:13.750 --> 01:30:15.190
Yeah, you got 44 of them back.

01:30:15.350 --> 01:30:16.870
So that's overkill.

01:30:16.950 --> 01:30:21.990
But all but Daz, who's standing up sufficiently high.

01:30:22.310 --> 01:30:22.789
Oh, shit.

01:30:23.590 --> 01:30:27.430
Begin to fall down a vast circular well.

01:30:28.950 --> 01:30:29.750
Plummeting.

01:30:31.190 --> 01:30:33.510
Can I grab the other two and open my wings?

01:30:34.230 --> 01:30:35.190
Hold on.

01:30:48.679 --> 01:30:51.239
I'm looking for an appropriate spell, but I'm not finding one.

01:30:51.399 --> 01:30:55.319
So I wave goodbye as he plummets.

01:30:58.449 --> 01:31:01.720
We'll see you at the bottom.

01:31:03.560 --> 01:31:06.920
Do I have any way to stop happening?

01:31:07.560 --> 01:31:18.760
While you guys are trying to figure out what spell to cast, while Grygum is holding, while Zalthir is using his strength to hold you guys, the two of you float.

01:31:19.720 --> 01:31:21.400
Can you describe the details?

01:31:21.720 --> 01:31:25.320
So, like, did the stairs turn into a slide and then they started to move?

01:31:25.480 --> 01:31:25.560
Yes.

01:31:25.880 --> 01:31:29.560
Or, like, is there debris in the well?

01:31:29.880 --> 01:31:30.520
Like, what's around?

01:31:30.840 --> 01:31:34.520
So, a 10-foot-long section of the stairs suddenly gives way.

01:31:35.159 --> 01:31:36.840
Gives way, like, starts to fall?

01:31:37.159 --> 01:31:37.880
Yes, falls.

01:31:37.960 --> 01:31:38.360
Yes.

01:31:38.680 --> 01:31:38.920
Okay.

01:31:39.720 --> 01:31:41.640
Am I okay on step 97?

01:31:42.600 --> 01:31:43.720
No, that's literally.

01:31:43.880 --> 01:31:54.039
No, what happens is that anybody standing between 101 and 90, no, 102 and 93 is caught in the hinge.

01:31:54.360 --> 01:31:56.119
So yes.

01:31:56.360 --> 01:32:01.720
So, and I can just use a regular action.

01:32:01.800 --> 01:32:03.480
Like, I can respond to this right away, right?

01:32:03.720 --> 01:32:04.600
Yes, yes.

01:32:04.920 --> 01:32:05.159
Okay.

01:32:05.400 --> 01:32:14.760
Well, then I would like to cast telekinesis and hold the stairs so that it does not fall.

01:32:15.400 --> 01:32:19.640
Or at least prevent it from falling anymore and then start moving back up.

01:32:20.280 --> 01:32:26.119
Make some dexterity saving throws just to see if you guys manage whether he caught it in time.

01:32:27.640 --> 01:32:28.360
Who makes the deck?

01:32:29.320 --> 01:32:30.200
So maybe no.

01:32:30.680 --> 01:32:31.320
16.

01:32:31.960 --> 01:32:32.440
16.

01:32:32.680 --> 01:32:35.240
Oh, they're dexterity saving throws.

01:32:35.480 --> 01:32:35.640
Okay.

01:32:36.840 --> 01:32:37.880
I think I okay.

01:32:38.680 --> 01:32:39.880
Give me a second here.

01:32:40.200 --> 01:32:40.440
So

01:32:43.550 --> 01:32:44.830
16, 27.

01:32:45.790 --> 01:32:46.910
Wait, did it do it?

01:32:47.230 --> 01:32:47.630
Damn it.

01:32:49.310 --> 01:32:50.110
It's not like.

01:32:51.230 --> 01:32:52.190
Oh, Grygum make it.

01:32:52.270 --> 01:32:52.990
Grygum made it.

01:32:55.719 --> 01:32:56.839
D20 minus one.

01:32:57.079 --> 01:32:59.799
Okay, so I got a three.

01:33:00.039 --> 01:33:00.199
What?

01:33:00.359 --> 01:33:05.399
I got two, but I can suffice it to say that.

01:33:08.599 --> 01:33:10.839
Okay, roll roll point.

01:33:13.079 --> 01:33:14.199
Oh, that time I got a five.

01:33:14.279 --> 01:33:15.159
That's so much better.

01:33:15.479 --> 01:33:15.799
All right.

01:33:15.960 --> 01:33:21.639
Well, as a result of that, but I'm presuming Daz will, sorry, Zalthir.

01:33:22.039 --> 01:33:24.679
So he starts to fall down the thing.

01:33:24.839 --> 01:33:30.920
The rest of you have managed to hold on to the stairs and I'm going to assume can scramble your way to safety.

01:33:31.000 --> 01:33:33.239
What do you want to do about Thorin who's falling?

01:33:33.559 --> 01:33:35.319
Well, I'm going to try one more time.

01:33:35.960 --> 01:33:41.239
I mean, you can re-roll it with a plus nine bonus, and then you must use the new role.

01:33:41.319 --> 01:33:45.479
So this would be a roll D20 plus eight.

01:33:46.119 --> 01:33:46.359
All right.

01:33:46.679 --> 01:33:47.479
Good luck.

01:33:47.799 --> 01:33:48.279
Or no.

01:33:48.599 --> 01:33:48.920
Okay.

01:33:49.960 --> 01:33:51.799
So, wait, plus nine.

01:33:52.039 --> 01:33:53.239
Yeah, plus eight.

01:33:53.479 --> 01:33:53.799
Okay.

01:33:58.369 --> 01:33:59.409
Oh, bad time.

01:34:00.449 --> 01:34:00.689
Big time.

01:34:01.649 --> 01:34:02.129
Big time off.

01:34:03.009 --> 01:34:03.250
Okay.

01:34:04.529 --> 01:34:05.089
Ah.

01:34:07.179 --> 01:34:07.500
Okay.

01:34:07.659 --> 01:34:09.259
So Mark Johnson sent me.

01:34:09.339 --> 01:34:11.899
I just want to leave this for Gabe because I'm sure he will enjoy it.

01:34:12.219 --> 01:34:18.779
Yeah, you told me about Greece retroactively revoking your degree, unless you mean there was a third.

01:34:21.019 --> 01:34:22.699
So given there was.

01:34:23.019 --> 01:34:23.899
There was another.

01:34:24.539 --> 01:34:25.420
There was another.

01:34:25.899 --> 01:34:26.699
Thank you.

01:34:27.979 --> 01:34:30.619
You're going to keep the style of speech going.

01:34:31.420 --> 01:34:31.899
There was another.

01:34:32.059 --> 01:34:32.379
Thank you.

01:34:32.460 --> 01:34:33.099
Thank you.

01:34:33.420 --> 01:34:34.460
Or there is another.

01:34:34.699 --> 01:34:35.019
I guess.

01:34:35.259 --> 01:34:35.819
It doesn't matter.

01:34:35.979 --> 01:34:36.939
There was, there is.

01:34:37.339 --> 01:34:38.219
Doesn't matter.

01:34:38.539 --> 01:34:53.019
Now, I just, he's very, he like, for those of you who don't know, whenever Mark wanted to give a speech about something he didn't want to do, he would point out that he quit high school without a degree because he was fed up with people telling him what to do.

01:34:55.899 --> 01:34:56.059
Yeah.

01:34:58.059 --> 01:35:02.859
And so we wanted to keep that in mind as we were telling him to do things that he didn't want to do.

01:35:04.379 --> 01:35:05.420
Yeah, that's Mark.

01:35:05.739 --> 01:35:07.259
Yeah, that was like a whole thing for him.

01:35:07.420 --> 01:35:13.579
So when I found out that my high school diploma was revoked by the Greek government, I kid you.

01:35:13.899 --> 01:35:14.139
What?

01:35:15.259 --> 01:35:22.699
So it turns out that I went to a school that had 13 years of high school because British schools do O-levels and A-levels.

01:35:23.099 --> 01:35:23.339
Yeah.

01:35:23.659 --> 01:35:25.179
And they did.

01:35:25.259 --> 01:35:26.139
They no longer do them.

01:35:26.619 --> 01:35:30.139
And so A-levels are essentially grades 12 and 13.

01:35:30.460 --> 01:35:30.939
Right.

01:35:31.899 --> 01:35:34.619
And so it has immortalized in Harry Potter.

01:35:34.859 --> 01:35:35.099
Yes.

01:35:35.420 --> 01:35:42.939
And so grade 12, they gave us a diploma at the end of grade 12 so that you could go to a U.S.

01:35:43.099 --> 01:35:46.460
college at grade 12 if you didn't want to spend the extra year to do the A-levels.

01:35:46.779 --> 01:35:52.379
And the Greek government had, the Greek government noticed that they had never actually sanctioned those degrees.

01:35:53.979 --> 01:35:55.099
And nobody had cared.

01:35:55.179 --> 01:35:59.179
But apparently in 2001, somebody cared.

01:35:59.739 --> 01:36:12.939
And as a result of that caring, they decided that it didn't count as a full high school degree, but it counted as if you had graduated from grade 11 from high school.

01:36:13.019 --> 01:36:18.059
And that's really important in Greece because there's a whole bunch of things that hinge on whether you have that degree or not.

01:36:18.379 --> 01:36:23.099
Not, you know, like in Greece, there's a lot more regulations and rules, et cetera, for everything.

01:36:23.579 --> 01:36:28.139
So yeah, so I told Mark that I too am a high school dropout.

01:36:30.460 --> 01:36:31.500
You didn't do the 13th year?

01:36:31.579 --> 01:36:32.460
Did you then go to a U.S.?

01:36:33.819 --> 01:36:36.139
I did do the 13th year, but I don't have a high school degree.

01:36:36.299 --> 01:36:38.379
So I bless myself.

01:36:39.019 --> 01:36:39.500
Wait, wait.

01:36:39.819 --> 01:36:42.059
But what do you get a degree after the 13th year?

01:36:42.139 --> 01:36:43.259
Wouldn't that be a high school degree?

01:36:43.339 --> 01:36:44.859
Or is that an A-levels degree?

01:36:45.179 --> 01:36:46.779
That's an A-levels thing.

01:36:47.099 --> 01:36:47.420
Okay.

01:36:47.819 --> 01:36:49.659
So this is just nomenclature here.

01:36:49.899 --> 01:36:50.379
Yes, yes.

01:36:50.539 --> 01:36:58.379
But I mean, with Mark, this was such a point of bragging that it's saying, I endured years of this.

01:37:00.139 --> 01:37:02.219
It amuses me he never brought it up in front of me.

01:37:03.179 --> 01:37:06.059
Yeah, but you were never trying to give him direction, whereas I, where I was.

01:37:06.379 --> 01:37:07.179
Well, yeah.

01:37:08.139 --> 01:37:17.099
I guess as someone who completed a PhD, it's hard to claim that I won't put up with any degree of bullshit.

01:37:18.139 --> 01:37:18.939
Exactly.

01:37:21.179 --> 01:37:27.979
But PhD, isn't that like doesn't it actually stand for I will put up with all kinds of bullshit?

01:37:28.539 --> 01:37:28.939
It does.

01:37:29.099 --> 01:37:29.259
Yeah.

01:37:29.500 --> 01:37:29.739
Yeah.

01:37:29.899 --> 01:37:32.299
It's it's Latin, but that's what it means.

01:37:35.179 --> 01:37:36.859
Yeah, Gabe, what happened at the gym?

01:37:37.500 --> 01:37:38.139
It's over there.

01:37:38.379 --> 01:37:40.379
Now it's its own huge room.

01:37:41.019 --> 01:37:42.379
Did you buy a new house?

01:37:42.699 --> 01:37:43.179
Yes.

01:37:43.500 --> 01:37:44.699
Oh, congratulations.

01:37:45.019 --> 01:37:45.339
Where?

01:37:45.579 --> 01:37:46.379
Thanks.

01:37:48.059 --> 01:37:48.699
Where?

01:37:49.659 --> 01:37:50.859
SF, Pac Heights.

01:37:51.179 --> 01:37:52.139
Gotcha.

01:37:52.859 --> 01:37:53.659
All right, folks.

01:37:53.979 --> 01:37:54.299
All right.

01:37:54.460 --> 01:37:56.379
And with that, we will end.

01:37:56.699 --> 01:37:56.939
All right.

01:37:57.019 --> 01:37:57.500
Have a good night.

01:37:57.579 --> 01:37:58.059
See y'all there.

01:37:58.699 --> 01:37:59.099
Good night.

01:37:59.179 --> 01:37:59.500
See you later.

